    {
      "id": "5d892c02-78d7-47d1-b349-70c8da5e531f",
      "name": "Note -820x-420",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -624,
        -416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Publish LinkedIn posts with images or video from one webhook\n\n**How it works**\n- A webhook receives `text` plus optional `image_urls` (1 to 20) or one `video_url`.\n- The workflow picks the route: text only, single image, multi-image post (Posts API) or native video (upload, then post).\n- Media is downloaded from your URLs and uploaded to LinkedIn, so nothing has to be stored first.\n- The response contains the public post URL, or HTTP 500 with LinkedIn's reason.\n\n**Setup steps**\n1. Create a LinkedIn app with the *Share on LinkedIn* product and an n8n **LinkedIn OAuth2 API** credential (scope `w_member_social`). Attach it to every LinkedIn HTTP node.\n2. In \"Set LinkedIn Settings\" enter your person ID as `author_id` (the `sub` value of `GET https://api.linkedin.com/v2/userinfo`).\n3. POST e.g. `{\"text\": \"Hello LinkedIn\", \"image_urls\": [\"https://example.com/a.png\"]}` to the webhook.\n\n**Good to know**\n- The native LinkedIn node cannot post multi-image carousels or native video, hence HTTP Request.\n- `Linkedin-Version` is a monthly API version. Update it in the settings node when LinkedIn retires yours.\n- Text is escaped for LinkedIn's \"little\" format, so `(`, `*` or `_` show up literally.\n- Protect the webhook with Header Auth before you expose it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a92e9dc8-2e23-42f3-9b08-2544af2cdac8",
      "name": "Note -20x-140",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -16,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 812,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and validate\nSettings and input checks run first, so a bad request fails fast with a readable error instead of half a post."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6a9419f6-3e67-40d5-9671-90b836a048e4",
      "name": "Note 900x-440",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        864,
        -432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1260,
        "height": 960,
        "content": "## 2. Upload media\nImages are registered with LinkedIn, downloaded from your URLs and uploaded one by one. A video uses the assets upload in a single request."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "437c0e60-50b6-481e-a0db-a835b98c2196",
      "name": "Note 2200x-140",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2208,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 940,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## 3. Create the post and respond\nPosts API for text and images, ugcPosts for video. Success counts only when LinkedIn returns a post ID. Every failure ends in one error response."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
